INSERT INTO "documents" ("key","body","updated_at","updated_by") VALUES('founder',replace('# The founder\n\nShri Ashok Kumar Bansal opened the workshop in 1993 with one bench, one safe and\na bound order book. By then, he had already spent years working in the jewellery\nindustry, learning the trade from the ground up and developing a deep\nunderstanding of craftsmanship, materials and the standards that good jewellery\ndemanded. He had no interest in retail as it was then practised — pieces bought\nin from elsewhere, marked up, and sold with a story attached.\n\nHis position was simple, and he never moved from it: if the house was going to\nput its name on a piece, the house would make it. Every commission from the first\nyear was drawn, cast, set and finished under his own supervision.\n\nThe second belief took longer for the trade to accept. He would tell a client not\nto buy. If the stone was wrong for the setting, if the occasion did not warrant\nthe expense, or if the family would be better served waiting a season — he said\nso. He was willing to lose the sale rather than compromise his judgement, and in\ndoing so, he earned something far more valuable: the family''s trust.\n\nThat standard became the foundation of Bansal Sons.\n\nHis legacy was carried forward by his sons, Chetan and Karan, and his son Rajeev,\nwho continue to work with the same principles that defined the house from its\nbeginning. The same floor, the same attention to detail, and the same belief that\na jeweller''s name must stand behind every piece that leaves the house.\n\nMany of the families who walked through the doors in those first years still do.\nToday, their children and grandchildren come to the same house — a quiet\ncontinuation of a trust that has passed from one generation to the next.\n\n<!-- IMAGE: replace. NO name caption on this photograph. Do not write\n     "Shri Ashok Kumar Bansal — at the bench, 1993". -->','\n',char(10)),'2026-09-01 18:02:49',NULL);
INSERT INTO "documents" ("key","body","updated_at","updated_by") VALUES('visit',replace('# What a visit is like\n\nGreeted by a member of the family, made comfortable, then introduced to each\npiece — one at a time, with the attention it deserves.\n\nWe tell you what you are seeing, how it was made, and what it costs.\n\nThe piece is weighed, billed and presented to you at the table.\n\nAnd before it leaves our hands, it receives a blessing.\n\n## The room\n\nGrey Italian marble underfoot, black marble on the feature walls, and light from above. Nine seating areas, so a conversation is never overheard, and one private cabin for the occasions that call for it. Nothing is behind glass you cannot ask to hold.','\n',char(10)),'2026-09-01 18:02:49',NULL);
INSERT INTO "documents" ("key","body","updated_at","updated_by") VALUES('pricing',replace('# How a price is built\n\nEvery bill we issue is itemised. Before you decide anything, you are told which of\nthe following applies and what it comes to.\n\n**Metal value** — the weight of gold or platinum in the piece, multiplied by the\nbullion rate at the moment. The rate we use is the published bullion rate at the\ntime of billing. Weight is taken in front of you.\n\n**Making charges** — the labour of the bench. These vary according to how the\npiece is made, reflecting the time, skill and craftsmanship involved — from\nmachine-made chain and lighter work to hand-set jadau and polki.\n\n- Machine-made and light gold\n- Standard handmade\n- Polki, kundan and jadau\n- Bespoke commissions: quoted per piece at the sketch stage\n\n**Stone value** — quoted separately and per stone, with the certificate attached.\nWhere a stone has been treated, that is stated in writing before it is set.\n\n**Wastage** — the unavoidable material loss that occurs during the manufacturing\nprocess. Gold and other precious metals are cut, filed, shaped, soldered and\npolished at the bench, and small amounts can be lost as dust, filings, fragments\nand material removed during finishing. Wastage reflects this genuine manufacturing\nloss and is charged transparently rather than being concealed within the price of\nthe piece.\n\n**GST** — charged at the prevailing rate on the invoice total, shown as a separate\nline.\n\n## What we do not do\n\nWe do not quote a single all-in figure and leave you to guess what is inside it.\nWe do not change the rate between the quote and the bill. We do not charge for the\nsketch, the CAD render, or the consultation.','\n',char(10)),'2026-09-01 18:02:49',NULL);
INSERT INTO "documents" ("key","body","updated_at","updated_by") VALUES('aftercare',replace('# Aftercare, buyback and exchange\n\n## Free, for life, on anything we have made\n\n- Cleaning and polishing\n- Rhodium re-plating on white gold\n- Tightening of settings and claws\n- Ring resizing\n- Restringing of pearl and bead work\n\nIf gold is required for any sizing, repair or finishing, the gold used will be\nchargeable.\n\n## Chargeable\n\n- Replacement of a lost stone, charged at the stone cost\n- Structural repair after damage, quoted at the bench\n- Remodelling into a new piece, quoted as a commission\n- Work on pieces not made by us, quoted after inspection\n\n## Turnaround\n\n<!-- Each line renders ONLY if its figure is present. With every figure absent,\n     this entire section (heading, intro and list) does not render. Replace a\n     [TK] with a number and that line - and the section - appears automatically. -->\n\nWe publish these because nobody else does, and because a vague promise of\n"lifetime service" is worth nothing without a timeframe attached.\n\n- Cleaning and polishing — `[TK]` working days\n- Resizing — `[TK]` working days\n- Claw and setting repair — `[TK]` working days\n- Restringing — `[TK]` working days\n- Stone replacement — quoted after inspection\n\nIf we expect to exceed the stated turnaround, you are told when you hand the piece\nover.\n\n## Buyback\n\nWe buy back all pieces we have made.\n\nYou receive the full value of the metal originally bought from us, based on its\napplicable metal value at the time of buyback.\n\n## Exchange\n\nExchange your piece for a new one.\n\nStones are not returned or credited on exchange, except diamonds, which are valued\nseparately.','\n',char(10)),'2026-09-01 18:02:49',NULL);
INSERT INTO "documents" ("key","body","updated_at","updated_by") VALUES('commission-terms',replace('# Commissioning a piece — the terms, before you come in\n\nMost houses explain a commission emotionally and leave the terms until you are\nalready sitting down. We would rather you read them first.\n\n## What it costs to start\n\nNothing. The consultation, the sketch and the CAD render are free, and remain free\nif you decide not to proceed.\n\n## The deposit\n\n30% of the quoted total, taken once you approve the design and we begin buying\nmetal and stones. It is credited against the final bill.\n\nNo advances are required if you are a regular.\n\n## Changes\n\nChanges to the design are included at no additional charge, whether made at the\nsketch stage or after work has begun. We believe the piece should be right before\nit is yours — so there are no charges for revisions.\n\n## Cancellation\n\nBefore casting: the deposit is returned in full, less the cost of any stones\nalready bought to your specification.\n\n<!-- UNANSWERED: what happens on cancellation after casting has begun? The\n     previous draft had a placeholder here and the client review did not address\n     it. Leave the section ending above until answered. -->\n\n## Delivery\n\nWe quote a completion date at the sketch stage and hold to it within the two to\nfour week window. If we are going to be late, you hear it from us before the date,\nnot after.\n\n## Who owns the design\n\nOne vision. One creation. Entirely yours.\n\n<!-- UNANSWERED: the "If it is wrong" section (remake standard) was specced and\n     not addressed in the client review. Omit it rather than invent a standard. -->\n\n## What we will not make\n\nWe will say no to a commission if the design will not survive being worn, if the\nstone is wrong for the setting, or if we do not believe we are the right house for\nit. You will be told why, and told who might be better placed.','\n',char(10)),'2026-09-01 18:02:49',NULL);
INSERT INTO "documents" ("key","body","updated_at","updated_by") VALUES('privacy',replace('# Privacy\n\nShort version: we collect only what we need to reply to you, we do not sell it,\nand we do not share it.\n\n## What the appointment form collects\n\nYour name, phone number, and — if you choose to give them — your email address,\npreferred date and time, the occasion, what you are interested in, an optional\nbudget range, and anything you write in the requirement box.\n\n## What happens to it\n\nIt is emailed to us and stored in our content system so we can prepare for your\nvisit. It is visible to the family and to the two members of staff who manage\nappointments. Nothing more.\n\n## How long we keep it\n\n12 months after your appointment, or until you ask us to delete it, whichever\nis sooner.\n\n## What we do not do\n\nWe do not sell, rent or share your details with anyone. We do not add you to a\nmarketing list unless you separately ask for the journal. We do not use tracking\ncookies or advertising pixels; our analytics are cookieless and count page views\nwithout identifying you.\n\n## Contacting you\n\nWe contact you once to confirm the appointment and once on the day. We do not\ncall after that.\n\n## Deleting your details\n\nWrite to bansalsonsjewellers18@gmail.com or call +91 85272 92840 and we will\ndelete everything we hold. No reason is needed.\n\n<!-- REPLACE: needs review against India''s Digital Personal Data Protection Act,\n     2023, including the grievance officer requirement. -->','\n',char(10)),'2026-09-01 18:02:49',NULL);
